GPGPU
The easiest way to use a GPU in Julia is through a high level interface. CUDA.jl, KernelAbstractions.jl, JACC.jl and Reactant.jl each offer such interfaces. For quite some time, and perhaps still, Nvidia GPUs and their CUDA library have dominated general purpose GPU (GPGPU) computing. However, AMD, Intel, Apple, Google, and Amazon now have similar software and hardware. CUDA.jl is Nvidia specific, while the other libraries work on a range of hardware.
We will often focus on CUDA.jl in these notes. CUDA.jl relies on Nvidia’s CUDA platform, so it only works with Nvidia GPUs. Nvidia tends to dominate GPGPU, and the GPUs available on Digitial Research Alliance of Canada servers are Nvidia.

Array interface
One way to use the GPU is with arrays.
using CUDA, Reactant, JACC, Random, BenchmarkTools
Reactant.set_default_backend("cuda")
#JACC.set_backend("CUDA")
JACC.@init_backend


N = 1000
M = 10000

function arraydemo(N,M)
    # wrapped in a  function so that the CuArrays are freed
    # otherwise we will run out GPU memory later
    A = randn(N,M);
    b = randn(M,2);
    println("Time on CPU")
    function foo(A,b)
        (A.^2)*b
    end
    @time c=foo(A,b);
    @time c=foo(A,b);

    println("Computations on the GPU with CUDA.jl")
    A_gpu = CuArray(A); # copy of A in GPU memory
    b_gpu = CuArray(b);
    # @btime does not work inside a function
    @time CUDA.@sync c_gpu=foo(A_gpu,b_gpu);
    @time CUDA.@sync c_gpu=foo(A_gpu,b_gpu);

    println("Computations on the GPU with JACC.jl")
    A_jacc = JACC.array(A)
    b_jacc = JACC.array(b)
    @time c_jacc = (foo(A_jacc, b_jacc), JACC.synchronize());
    @time c_jacc = (foo(A_jacc, b_jacc), JACC.synchronize());


    println("Computations on the TPU/GPU via XLA with Reactant.jl")
    A_react = Reactant.ConcreteRArray(A)
    b_react = Reactant.ConcreteRArray(b)
    # Precompile with Reactant to get accurate timing for the second run
    foo_react = Reactant.@compile sync=true foo(A_react, b_react)
    @time c_react = foo_react(A_react, b_react);
    @time c_react = foo_react(A_react, b_react);

    println("But copying to and from GPU takes time")
    bar(A,b) =Array(foo(CuArray(A), CuArray(b)))
    @time c2=bar(A,b);
    @time c2=bar(A,b);
end
